diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..587fdf1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# fluent
+
+Local real-time transcription and translation web app for meetings and
+interviews. Single user, single machine: the server binds to `127.0.0.1`,
+there is no auth layer, and all data stays on your disk except audio/text
+sent to the STT and LLM APIs you configure.
+
+## Features
+
+- Live English transcription with speaker diarization (Deepgram Nova-3 by
+  default; AssemblyAI as a low-cost path without diarization).
+- Segment-by-segment translation into a user-selected target language via
+  any OpenAI-compatible LLM (DeepSeek by default, optional fallback
+  provider).
+- Optional WAV recording of the session audio, with playback-synced
+  transcript review.
+- Sessions stored as local Markdown files (frontmatter metadata) plus a
+  bilingual `.srt` export. No database.
+- Answer-assist: LLM-generated suggested answers for interview-style
+  sessions.
+- Cost: roughly $0.60-0.70 per audio hour on the default diarized path
+  (see `scripts/estimate-cost.ts`). Bring your own API keys.
+
+## Quickstart
+
+```bash
+cp .env.example .env   # fill in DEEPGRAM_API_KEY (or ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY)
+                       # and LLM_API_KEY
+npm install
+npm --prefix web install
+npm run dev            # backend on :3000, Vite dev UI on :5173
+```
+
+Production mode:
+
+```bash
+npm run build:web
+npm start              # serves API + built UI on http://127.0.0.1:3000
+```
+
+Tests and checks:
+
+```bash
+npm test               # vitest
+npm run typecheck      # tsc --noEmit
+```
